T Technology substrate T1 stone/organic; T2 metallurgy; T3 writing/bureaucracy; T4 print; T5 industrial; T6 digital/open protocol

9.2 Compatibility Constraints

Definition 9.1. The compatibility relation C is specified by the following constraint families:

1. Technological coherence: T_1 (stone/organic) cannot support I_5 (networked digital) or D_6 (liquid/sortition at scale).
2. Scale coherence: N_1 (band) cannot support R_6 (central allocation) or P_5 (centralized sovereign).
3. Allocation-decision coherence: R_6 (central allocation) and D_5 (market/price) are compatible only with a dual-track mechanism.
4. Power-decision coherence: P_5 (centralized sovereign) and D_1 (consensus) are compatible only with federated structure.

Open problem: The full compatibility relation has not been specified. We estimate |\mathcal{P}| \approx 0.3 \times |\mathcal{P}_0| based on the density of incoherent combinations in a random sample. This is a target for empirical validation.

9.3 Ontology JSON

The ontology is specified as machine-readable JSON in Appendix B. Each modality object contains: dimension, modality, label, short_def, formal_definition, inclusion_criteria, exclusion_criteria, boundary_cases, disambiguation, DPLACE_vars, Seshat_vars, historical_examples, measurement, coder_notes, overlap_flags.

