Appendix D — Bayesian Occupancy Model

D.1 Hierarchical Specification

Likelihood. For s \in \mathcal{P}_{RDP}:

O(s) \mid Z(s) \sim \text{Bernoulli}(Z(s) \cdot p_{\text{det}}(s))

Prior. Z(s) \mid \psi(s) \sim \text{Bernoulli}(\psi(s)) with

\text{logit}(\psi(s)) = \alpha + \beta_1 X_1(s) + \beta_2 X_2(s) + \beta_3 X_3(s)

where:

· X_1(s): compatibility score (fraction of pairwise constraints satisfied)
· X_2(s): complexity (number of dimensions deviating from modal historical values)
· X_3(s): resource requirement estimate

Detection. p_{\text{det}}(s) = \text{logit}^{-1}(\gamma_0 + \gamma_1 \cdot \text{DocIntensity}(s)) where DocIntensity is a proxy for research coverage.

Hyperpriors.

\alpha \sim \mathcal{N}(0, 1), \quad \beta_i \sim \mathcal{N}(0, 1), \quad \gamma_0, \gamma_1 \sim \mathcal{N}(0, 1).

D.2 Inference

We recommend Hamiltonian Monte Carlo via Stan or NumPyro for the 216-cell model. The model is small; full posterior sampling requires minutes on CPU.

```python
# numpyro sketch
import numpyro
import numpyro.distributions as dist
from numpyro.infer import MCMC, NUTS

def occupancy_model(O, X, DocIntensity):
    alpha = numpyro.sample("alpha", dist.Normal(0, 1))
    beta  = numpyro.sample("beta",  dist.Normal(0, 1).expand([X.shape[1]]).to_event(1))
    gamma0 = numpyro.sample("gamma0", dist.Normal(0, 1))
    gamma1 = numpyro.sample("gamma1", dist.Normal(0, 1))

    psi = numpyro.deterministic("psi",
        jax.nn.sigmoid(alpha + X @ beta))
    p_det = jax.nn.sigmoid(gamma0 + gamma1 * DocIntensity)

    with numpyro.plate("cells", len(O)):
        Z = numpyro.sample("Z", dist.Bernoulli(psi), infer={"enumerate": "parallel"})
        numpyro.sample("O", dist.Bernoulli(Z * p_det), obs=O)

mcmc = MCMC(NUTS(occupancy_model), num_warmup=1000, num_samples=2000)
mcmc.run(rng_key, O=obs, X=X, DocIntensity=doc)
```

D.3 Posterior Predictive Checks

For each cell, compute:

· \pi(s): posterior occupancy probability
· 95% credible interval for \psi(s)
· Posterior predictive observation frequency

D.4 Reporting

Report:

1. N_{\text{obs}}^{0.95} = |\{s : \pi(s) > 0.95\}|
2. Heatmap of \pi(s) across the 216-cube
3. Covariate effects \beta

